    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0180" n="166" xml:id="pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/3908a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Cuba</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-28T17:00:00-04:00">May 28, 1943—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>624. From Brown,<anchor n="91" xml:id="d156-f1"/> CCC. You are requested to make
                    a firm offer to the Cuban Sugar Stabilization Institute for the 300,000 tons of
                    free sugar produced in Cuba during the 1943 crop,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d156-f2"
                    /> under the same terms as governed the purchase of the 2,700,000 tons. If
                    accepted you are authorized to exchange letters immediately so that June first
                    payment can include this sugar, providing that the Institute can issue proper
                    identity certificates by that date. [Brown.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d156-f1" n="91" xml:id="d156-f1-content">
                <p>Courtney Brown, vice president of the Commodity Credit Corporation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d156-f2" n="92" xml:id="d156-f2-content">
                <p>The Purchase Agreement on the 1943 sugar crop authorized the production of
                    300,000 short tons of raw sugar for sale in world markets, and granted to
                    Commodity Credit Corporation an option on its purchase.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
